BT /F1 10.5 Tf 50 790 Td 14.5 TL (ILLUSTRATIVE TEXT FOR TESTING - NOT AN OFFICIAL RWANDA FDA DOCUMENT) Tj T* () Tj T* (GUIDELINES ON THE COMMON TECHNICAL DOCUMENT \(CTD\) FOR HUMAN MEDICINES) Tj T* (Version 2026-01) Tj T* () Tj T* (1. Structure) Tj T* (Human medicine dossiers are submitted in CTD format, in five modules.) Tj T* () Tj T* (2. Module 1: Administrative information and prescribing information) Tj T* (Module 1 contains the regional administrative information and the prescribing information:) Tj T* (the summary of product characteristics \(SmPC\) and the patient information leaflet \(PIL\),) Tj T* (with the labelling.) Tj T* () Tj T* (3. Module 2: Summaries) Tj T* (Module 2 contains the quality overall summary, the non-clinical overview and the clinical) Tj T* (overview.) Tj T* () Tj T* (4. Module 3: Quality) Tj T* (Module 3 describes the active substance and the finished product. Section 3.2.P.8 must) Tj T* (contain stability data that support the proposed shelf life and storage conditions. The) Tj T* (duration of the long-term stability data must be at least as long as the proposed shelf) Tj T* (life, unless an extrapolation is justified.) Tj T* () Tj T* (5. Module 4: Non-clinical study reports) Tj T* (Module 4 contains the non-clinical study reports. For well-established active substances, a) Tj T* (literature-based non-clinical overview may be accepted.) Tj T* () Tj T* (6. Module 5: Clinical study reports) Tj T* (Module 5 contains the clinical study reports. For generic medicines, it must include a) Tj T* (bioequivalence study against the reference product, with the 90% confidence intervals of the) Tj T* (test/reference ratios for AUC and Cmax within 80.00-125.00%.) Tj T* ET
